/*
 * Declares the OperatorValue class.
 *
 * OperatorValue is the abstract ancestor of all operator value classes. It
 * represents the semantic result of applying an operator (unary, binary,
 * assignment, call, indexing, slicing, field access, ...) to one or more
 * operands. Concrete subclasses implement the behavior, typing rules, and
 * reduction logic of each operator form.
 *
 * Operator values participate in the generator’s reduction pipeline. Reduction
 * simplifies expressions as far as possible at compile time. This includes:
 *
 *   - constant folding,
 *   - operator simplification,
 *   - constant indexing and slicing,
 *   - compile-time constructor evaluation,
 *   - and inlining of functions marked `@inline`.
 *
 * Reduction does not imply compile-time evaluation. A reduced value may still
 * depend on runtime data or contain side effects. A value is a compile-time
 * constant only when reduction produces a full literal.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2025-01-04
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
